 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to acquire permanent easements through negotiation, condemnation and acceptance, for the Treemont Pump Station and Water Main project, for five properties located on Tyne Valley Boulevard, Brentview Drive and Tyne Ridge Court (Project No. 24-WC-9 and Proposal Nos. 2025M-117ES-001 and 2025M117ES-002). \n..body\nWHEREAS, the negotiation, condemnation and acceptance of permanent easements, for five properties located on Tyne Valley Boulevard, Brentview Drive and Tyne Ridge Court, are needed to construct MWS Project No. 24-WC-9; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2025M117ES-001 on July 22, 2025, and mandatory referral No. 2025M-117ES-002 on September 21, 2026, for the negotiation, condemnation and acceptance of permanent easements.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to negotiate, condemn, and accept permanent easements, for five properties located on Tyne Valley Boulevard, Brentview Drive and Tyne Ridge Court, as shown on Exhibits 1 through 6, which are attached hereto and incorporated by reference.\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the negotiation, condemnation and acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAll necessary and incidental cost of the temporary and permanent easements herein authorized to be accepted shall be paid from funds authorized from Fund No. 47410 /Capital Plan #124.\nSection 4.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 5.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance authorizes the negotiation, condemnation, and acceptance of permanent easements for the Treemont Pump Station and Water Main project for five properties located on Tyne Valley Boulevard, Brentview Drive and Tyne Ridge Court.\n\nThis has been approved by the Planning Commission. Future amendments to this legislation may be approved by resolution.\n"
}
